{"name":"Limonite","hex":"#be7f51","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"limonite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several natural hydrous iron oxides; often a mixture of goethite and hematite with clays and manganese oxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/limonite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Limonite","blocks":[{"text":"Limonite is an iron ore consisting of a mixture of hydrated iron(III) oxide-hydroxides in varying composition. The generic formula is frequently written as FeO(OH)·nH2O, although this is not entirely accurate as the ratio of oxide to hydroxide can vary quite widely. Limonite is one of the three principal iron ores, the others being hematite and magnetite, and has been mined for the production of iron since at least 400 BC."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/LimoniteUSGOV.jpg/330px-LimoniteUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limonite","wikidata":"Q193565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Limonite_bog_iron_cm01.jpg/500px-Limonite_bog_iron_cm01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Limonite_bog_iron_cm01.jpg/500px-Limonite_bog_iron_cm01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bog iron ore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALimonite_bog_iron_cm01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/La_Palma_Limonit.jpg/250px-La_Palma_Limonit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/La_Palma_Limonit.jpg/500px-La_Palma_Limonit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/La_Palma_Li